Story B: Many years ago there was a man named Alexander who had two wives living in two houses: He liked to boast to a friend that with his two wives he would always eat well. One day when he was very hungry, Alexander went to his first wife. But she had only prepared enough for herself and their baby. She thought Alexander would eat with his other wife that day. Alexander then went to his second wife, but found she had already finished. She saw him go to the other house so she thought he was eating there. Thus Alexander went without any dinner at all.

